 result←object New arg;parent;name;props;newobj;size;punits;units;extent;newtab;previous
 (parent name)←object ⍝ Separate non-standard two-part argument
 previous←'TabButton'##.##.∆WN parent

 newtab←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',##.##.Next parent)##.##.∆WC'TabButton' ⍝ First create a hidden "Tab" object using the next available arbitrary number
 ##.##.New.InitChild parent newtab

 props←'SubForm'('Visible' 0) ⍝ Define properties that must be used during "Page" creation
 newobj←⎕VGET(parent⍕⍛,'.',name)##.##.∆WC props ⍝ Create the actual Dyalog object with required parameters
 newobj ##.##.∆WS⊂'TabObj'newtab ⍝ Connect this to the hidden TabButton object created above
 newtab._Owner←newobj ⍝ Change the ownership of the TabButton to be this new SubForm (Page) so internal events fire properly

 ⍝ Explicitly set positioning variables before calling ∇Initialize, since they're not modifiable
 (punits units)←1 0 1/##._supp.MyUnits parent
 extent←parent._size ⋄ size←extent÷units[1;]÷punits ⍝ Occupy full client area of parent Selector
 newobj.(_where _extent _size)←(0 0,extent)extent size

 arg,←(~arg ##._supp.HasInitialProps'caption')/⊂'caption'name
 result←parent newobj ##.##.New.Initialize arg ⍝ Complete standard class-initialization procedure

 newtab ##.##.New.SysEvents newobj ⍝ Set up any system-level events (e.g. _on_Select) that need to come from the TabButton instead of the SubForm
 :If 0=≢previous ⋄ 1 ##.##.∆NQ newtab'Select' ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Force auto-selection of first-added page

 ⍝? Note: Adding a new Page to a Selector causes it to be automatically set in TabControl.TabObj. It should instead preserve the current tab, including "none".
